\b\f0 Role in Story:\b0\f1  Unseen but foundational figure. John's mother and one of the scientists whose work underpins the Serva Vitae project, the worker-bot era and the Beverly's legacy.\par
\b\f0 Goal:\b0\f1  Advance radical life-preserving technology beyond the limits of cautious institutions.\par
\b\f0 Physical Description:\b0\f1  Known mostly through photographs and memory rather than direct on-page appearance.\par
\b\f0 Personality:\b0\f1  Fearless, forceful, velocity-loving and hard to contain.\par
\b\f0 Occupation:\b0\f1  Professor, physicist and project scientist.\par
\b\f0 Habits/Mannerisms:\b0\f1  Holds her ground under pressure; the kind of person who can stare down a panicking horse or a political superior.\par
\b\f0 Background:\b0\f1  Worked with Ava and Wolfgang during the Serva Vitae period. John loses contact with her after the worker-bot program is decommissioned.\par
\b\f0 Internal Conflicts:\b0\f1  Her work appears to have taken precedence over family life, leaving distance between her and John.\par
\b\f0 External Conflicts:\b0\f1  Her research and personality repeatedly put her at odds with institutional control.\par
\b\f0 Notes:\b0\f1  The Beverly carries her legacy forward, both technically and symbolically.\par
